From: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: es8326: describe BCLK as main clock

Describe the optional BCLK main-clock source for boards without MCLK.
The machine driver supplies the BCLK rate as codec sysclk.

Signed-off-by: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/everest,es8326.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/everest,es8326.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,15 @@
   clock-names:
     items:
       - const: mclk
+
+  everest,bclk-as-mclk:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      Use the external BCLK input as the codec main clock instead of MCLK.
+      The codec must consume BCLK and LRCK. The machine driver must pass
+      the BCLK frequency as the codec sysclk and provide a BCLK/sample-rate
+      ratio supported by the codec clock table, for example 64 with two
+      32-bit I2S slots. An external MCLK is not required in this mode.
 
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
